Partition strict and shared homologs

Run the example commands from the top-level project directory. Adapt input paths to your files. Use BLAST+, BEDTools and SAMtools as required, or activate the environment defined in environment.yml.

1. Split nuclear intervals into strict NUMHs, strict NUPHs, and shared nuclear–mitochondrial–plastid homologs. The three sets are mutually exclusive at the base level.

    bedtools subtract -a mt.bed -b pt.bed > strict_NUMH.bed
    bedtools subtract -a pt.bed -b mt.bed > strict_NUPH.bed
    bedtools intersect -a mt.bed -b pt.bed |
      bedtools sort -i - | bedtools merge -i - > shared.bed

2. Count intervals and sum their lengths. Sum across haplotypes for accession totals and divide by accession ploidy for haploid-equivalent values.

    awk '{n++; bp+=$3-$2} END{print n+0, bp+0}' strict_NUMH.bed
